    description: "**CLUSTER tranch03-cluster-003 (MED confidence) — members F52.A1 + F53.A1.**\n\n**Mechanic**: Edge `meta` dicts on the self-corpus carry keys like `evidence_type`, `access_mode`, `call_construct`, `resolution_quality`, `framework_dispatch` — but `io_boundary` never appears. The substrate has 61,906 `calls` edges; zero carry an `io_boundary` key. The classification logic exists, but is computed on-the-fly from the io_primitives YAML catalogs at consumer-time inside the `io-boundaries` CLI — never persisted into the behavior map. The spec's controlled vocabulary (`fs_read`, `fs_write`, `net_send`, etc.) appears nowhere in the substrate. The companion `slice --io-boundary <category>` flag promised by the spec at three separate doc references (with a verbatim example in the architecture decision record) is entirely unimplemented: not in the CLI parser, not handled in the slice command, no source reference anywhere. Both consumer affordances — read the persisted field directly OR filter slices by category — are absent.\n\n**Expectation**: Either `meta.io_boundary` is stamped at producer time per the spec contract and `slice --io-boundary <category>` is a working CLI affordance, or the spec is updated to admit that the on-the-fly `io-boundaries` CLI is the canonical surface and the persistence/filter promises are removed.\n\n**Scope**: Persistence: 110,533 of 110,533 edges with null `meta.io_boundary`. Filter: zero of three documented call sites for the `--io-boundary` flag have a working implementation; the verbatim spec example exits with `unrecognized arguments`.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer reading `edge.meta.io_boundary` directly per the spec; any consumer running the verbatim spec example for slice-by-boundary; any agent composing `--io-boundary` with the other slice filters (`--max-tier`, `--exclude-tests`, `--reverse`).\n\n**Consequence**: The IO-boundary feature ships in name only — neither the persisted field nor the slice filter is available; the only path to io-boundary-filtered information is a separate CLI command that emits primitives-and-chains rather than a nodes/edges slice graph and does not compose with the documented slice flags. Tier 3-4 on the documented `slice` contract.\n\n**Source**: CLUSTER (F52.A1 + F53.A1, MED). One pillar-completion effort addresses both persistence and filter gaps.\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 15fe
    fields: {}  # 15fe
